  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Solve the inequality $-10\\cdot {5}^{2-7x}+3x\\cdot {5}^{2-7x}>-{5}^{2-7x}{x}^{2}.$\n\n$x<${{field-1}}\n$\\,\\text{or}\\,x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10\\cdot {5}^{2-7x}+3x\\cdot {5}^{2-7x} & >-{5}^{2-7x}{x}^{2} \\\\ {5}^{2-7x}{x}^{2}-10\\cdot {5}^{2-7x}+3x\\cdot {5}^{2-7x} & >0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+3x-10){5}^{2-7x} & >0 \\\\ (x+5)(x-2){5}^{2-7x} & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${5}^{2-7x}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+5)(x-2){5}^{2-7x}}{{5}^{2-7x}} & >\\frac{0}{{5}^{2-7x}} \\\\ (x+5)(x-2) & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=-5$ and $x=2.$ The parabola is above the $x$-axis when $x<-5$ or $x>2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/assets/6b72efca34700ab06986460d4d190e0e83a4f0068c9effe20af622082a92b9a9.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $x<-5$ or $x>2.$",
